# model-rust auto

Complementary to `/note` (Mongo `notes`) — **not a second `/note`**. Auto chat/ops under collection **`turns`** (source=`chat`). Durable decisions → `/note` (`note add`); auto turn transcript → hooks.

## When

Auto applies to **every submitted Agent prompt** (length ≥ 6), not only slash skills.
Skip short acks (`ok` / `yes` / `ยืนยัน` / …). Not every keystroke.

Hooks (workspace `.cursor/hooks.json`) stage prompt + response and **`add` on stop**
(`source=chat`, tags include `auto` + skill-or-`chat`).

Activity log (proof it ran): `.cursor/hooks/state/model-rust-auto.log`

Disable: `MODEL_RUST_AUTO=0` or `.cursor/hooks/state/model-rust-auto.off`.

## Project (AI sets — never hardcode)

Resolve `PROJECT` slug `[a-z0-9-]+` like `/note` (user name → git/app folder → pack work → ask once).

On every substantive reply include one short line so hooks can stamp the turn:

```text
MODEL-RUST-PROJECT: <slug>
```

If missing, hooks save the turn with `project: null`. Do **not** default to `agent-skills` unless the work is actually about this pack.

## Agent must do (visible)

1. **Recall** at start of substantive work (pass `--project` when known):

```powershell
agent-skills\model-rust\target\debug\model-rust.exe search --q "<keywords>" --project <slug> --limit 5
```

Cite `MODEL-RUST: …` (or `MODEL-RUST: none`).

2. **Persist** — hooks own `add` on `stop` (project from `MODEL-RUST-PROJECT:`). Agent `add` only when the log shows `FAIL`/`SKIP` or hooks are disabled:

Write `agent-skills/model-rust/tmp/last.json` then:

```powershell
agent-skills\model-rust\target\debug\model-rust.exe add --json agent-skills\model-rust\tmp\last.json
```

Include `source: "chat"`, tags `["auto", …]`, and **`project` you resolved**. Never store secrets/URI/PII dumps.

3. Reply lines: `MODEL-RUST-PROJECT: <slug>` · optional `MODEL-RUST-SAVE: <turn id or reason>`.

## Commands

| Cmd | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `ping` | connectivity |
| `search -q …` | ≤5 short hits |
| `get --id …` | one turn |
| `add --json …` | insert turn |
| `note …` | durable notes |
